---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Latvian Blues Band"
  description="Privacy policy for latvianbluesband.lv — how we collect, use, and protect your personal data under GDPR."
>
  <Navbar homeBase="/" />

  <main class="privacy-main" id="main-content">
    <div class="privacy-content">
      <header class="privacy-header">
        <p class="privacy-eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="privacy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="privacy-meta">Last updated: 25 May 2026</p>
        <p class="privacy-intro">
          This policy explains what personal data latvianbluesband.lv collects,
          why, and what rights you have over it. We've kept it plain — no legal
          boilerplate that doesn't apply to us.
        </p>
      </header>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <!-- 1. WHO WE ARE -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p>
          Latvian Blues Band is a music group based in Latvia. We are the data
          controller for personal data collected through this website.
        </p>
        <div class="info-block">
          <p>
            <strong>Data controller:</strong>
            <span class="placeholder">Viesturs Grapmanis</span>
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Email for privacy requests:</strong>
            <span class="placeholder">info@itvgsolutions.lv</span>
          </p>
          <p><strong>Website:</strong> latvianbluesband.lv</p>
        </div>
        <p>
          We do not have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) — our processing is not
          large-scale or systematic in a way that requires one under GDPR
          Article 37.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. WHAT DATA WE COLLECT -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>2. What Data We Collect</h2>

        <h3>2.1 Newsletter (Mailchimp)</h3>
        <p>
          When you subscribe to our newsletter, we collect your <strong
            >email address</strong
          >. Mailchimp — our email service provider — also automatically records
          your signup timestamp, IP address, approximate location, and email
          engagement metrics (whether you open emails or click links).
        </p>
        <p>
          This is the only form on the site. Subscription is entirely voluntary.
        </p>

        <h3>2.2 Website Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</h3>
        <p>
          <em>Google Analytics is not yet active on this site.</em> When it is enabled,
          GA4 will collect: approximate location (city-level, derived from your IP
          address — full IPs are not stored), device type, browser, pages visited,
          session duration, and how you arrived at the site. This data is anonymous
          and aggregate — we cannot identify you individually from it.
        </p>
        <p>
          GA4 uses cookies. We will implement a cookie consent banner before
          activating analytics — it will not run without your explicit opt-in.
        </p>

        <h3>2.3 Hosting Logs (Netlify)</h3>
        <p>
          Our hosting provider, Netlify, automatically logs standard server
          access data including IP addresses and browser information. This is a
          normal part of operating any website and is handled by Netlify, not us
          directly.
        </p>

        <h3>2.4 Email Contact (Booking)</h3>
        <p>
          The booking link on this site opens your own email application via a <code
            >mailto:</code
          > link. We collect nothing through this — your email client handles it entirely.
        </p>

        <h3>2.5 Embedded Media (Spotify, YouTube)</h3>
        <p>
          This site includes Spotify and YouTube players. These embeds are
          loaded from Spotify's and Google's servers. When you interact with
          them, those services may set their own cookies and collect usage data
          under their own privacy policies. We have no control over or access to
          that data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. LEGAL BASIS -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>3. Why We Collect It (Legal Basis)</h2>

        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table class="policy-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Data</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Legal basis (GDPR Art. 6)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Newsletter email + engagement</td>
                <td>Sending news, show announcements, and updates</td>
                <td>Consent — Art. 6(1)(a)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Analytics data (when active)</td>
                <td
                  >Understanding how people use the site so we can improve it</td
                >
                <td>Consent — Art. 6(1)(a)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Hosting server logs</td>
                <td>Operating, securing, and troubleshooting the website</td>
                <td>Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p>
          You can withdraw consent for the newsletter at any time using the
          unsubscribe link at the bottom of every email. You can withdraw
          consent for analytics by declining or withdrawing cookie consent
          through the cookie preference tool (available when GA4 is activated).
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. WHO WE SHARE DATA WITH -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>4. Who We Share Data With</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell your data. We share it only with the service providers
          necessary to run this site.
        </p>

        <h3>4.1 Mailchimp (Intuit Inc., USA)</h3>
        <p>
          Your newsletter subscription is stored and managed by Mailchimp.
          Mailchimp acts as a data processor on our behalf under a Data
          Processing Addendum (DPA) that incorporates Standard Contractual
          Clauses. Mailchimp also inserts tracking pixels in emails to record
          open rates — this is standard email marketing practice and covered by
          the consent you give when subscribing.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a
            href="https://mailchimp.com/legal/privacy/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="policy-link"
          >
            Mailchimp Privacy Policy →
          </a>
        </p>

        <h3>4.2 Google LLC (USA)</h3>
        <p>
          When Google Analytics 4 is active, usage data is sent to Google and
          processed under Google's Data Processing Terms. Google acts as a data
          processor.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="policy-link"
          >
            Google Privacy Policy →
          </a>
        </p>

        <h3>4.3 Netlify Inc. (USA)</h3>
        <p>
          This website is hosted on Netlify, which processes server access logs
          as part of normal hosting operations. Netlify acts as a data processor
          under their Data Processing Agreement, which includes Standard
          Contractual Clauses.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a
            href="https://www.netlify.com/gdpr-ccpa/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="policy-link"
          >
            Netlify GDPR &amp; Privacy →
          </a>
        </p>

        <h3>4.4 Spotify and YouTube</h3>
        <p>
          Embedded players load content directly from Spotify's and Google's
          servers. Any data collected through those embeds is governed by their
          own policies, which we link to above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. INTERNATIONAL TRANSFERS -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>5. International Transfers</h2>
        <p>
          All three of our service providers (Mailchimp, Google, Netlify) are
          headquartered in the United States. Transfers of your personal data to
          the US are protected by two mechanisms:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>EU–US Data Privacy Framework (DPF):</strong> Both Mailchimp (Intuit)
            and Google are certified under the DPF, which the European Commission
            recognized as providing adequate protection in its July 2023 adequacy
            decision. The EU General Court upheld this decision in September 2025.
            An appeal is pending at the Court of Justice of the EU (Case C-703/25
            P) — the outcome remains uncertain.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs):</strong> All three processors
            have SCCs incorporated into their Data Processing Agreements as a backup
            transfer mechanism, valid regardless of the DPF's status.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. RETENTION -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>6. How Long We Keep Your Data</h2>

        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table class="policy-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Data</th>
                <th>Retention period</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Newsletter subscription</td>
                <td
                  >Until you unsubscribe (you can do this at any time via any
                  email we send)</td
                >
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Analytics data</td>
                <td
                  >14 months (Google Analytics default, as configured in our GA4
                  property settings)</td
                >
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Hosting server logs</td>
                <td>Per Netlify's operational retention policy</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. YOUR RIGHTS -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>7. Your Rights Under GDPR</h2>
        <p>
          Under GDPR, you have the following rights regarding your personal
          data:
        </p>

        <ul class="rights-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal data we hold
            about you
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Rectification</strong> — ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete
            data
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Erasure</strong> — ask us to delete your data (the "right to be
            forgotten")
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Restriction</strong> — ask us to pause processing while a dispute
            is resolved
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Portability</strong> — receive your data in a machine-readable
            format
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Objection</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate
            interest
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — for the newsletter, use the unsubscribe
            link in any email; for analytics, use the cookie preference tool
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, email us at:
          <span class="placeholder">info@itvgsolutions.lv</span>. We will
          respond within one month as required by GDPR.
        </p>

        <div class="dvi-block">
          <p>
            You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Latvian Data
            State Inspectorate (<em>Datu valsts inspekcija</em>, DVI) — the
            supervisory authority for data protection in Latvia:
          </p>
          <p>
            <a
              href="https://www.dvi.gov.lv/en"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="policy-link"
            >
              dvi.gov.lv →
            </a>
          </p>
          <p class="dvi-address">Elijas iela 17, Riga, LV-1050, Latvia</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. COOKIES -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          A cookie is a small text file stored in your browser. Here is what
          this site sets and why:
        </p>

        <div class="table-wrapper">
          <table class="policy-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Source</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Status</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Google Analytics 4</td>
                <td
                  >Site usage analytics (pages visited, session data, traffic
                  source)</td
                >
                <td
                  >Not yet active — will require your explicit opt-in consent
                  when enabled</td
                >
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Spotify</td>
                <td>Music player functionality</td>
                <td>Only set when you interact with the Spotify player</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>YouTube (Google)</td>
                <td>Video player functionality</td>
                <td>Only set when you interact with the YouTube player</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p>
          Analytics cookies are non-essential under the ePrivacy Directive and
          cannot be loaded without your prior consent. We will implement a
          cookie consent tool before activating Google Analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can manage or delete cookies at any time through your browser
          settings. Removing cookies does not affect your ability to use this
          site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. CHILDREN -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>9. Children</h2>
        <p>
          This website is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly
          collect personal data from anyone under that age. If you believe a
          child has subscribed to the newsletter without appropriate consent,
          please contact us at the email above and we will delete their data
          promptly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 10. CHANGES -->
      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy when our data practices change or when legal
          requirements require it. The "Last updated" date at the top of this
          page will reflect any revisions. For material changes, we will add a
          note to the website.
        </p>
        <p>
          Continued use of the site after a policy update does not constitute
          consent to the changes — please review the policy periodically.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <p class="back-link-wrap">
        <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to latvianbluesband.lv</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-main {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--color-bg-deep);
    padding-top: 64px; /* navbar height */
  }

  .privacy-content {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem 5rem;
  }

  /* Header */
  .privacy-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .privacy-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .privacy-title {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .privacy-meta {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .privacy-intro {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }

  /* Divider */
  .divider {
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  /* Sections */
  .policy-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .policy-section h2 {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", serif;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .policy-section h3 {
    font-family: "Source Sans 3", sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .policy-section p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .policy-section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-section ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .policy-section li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .policy-section strong {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .policy-section em {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .policy-section code {
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.875em;
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  /* Info block */
  .info-block {
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .info-block p {
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem !important;
  }

  /* Placeholder text — owner must replace */
  .placeholder {
    background: rgba(196, 132, 45, 0.12);
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: 0.875em;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Tables */
  .table-wrapper {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .policy-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .policy-table th {
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-family: "Source Sans 3", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .policy-table td {
    padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .policy-table tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  /* Rights list */
  .rights-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 0;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .rights-list li {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .rights-list li::before {
    content: "–";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* DVI block */
  .dvi-block {
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .dvi-block p {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem !important;
  }

  .dvi-address {
    font-size: 0.82rem !important;
    margin-top: 0.25rem !important;
  }

  /* Links */
  .policy-link {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* Back link */
  .back-link-wrap {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .privacy-content {
      padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem;
    }

    .policy-table th,
    .policy-table td {
      padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
